    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0410" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg312"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 687.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your two cables concerning our attitude in
                    China were received on the 2d<anchor n="2" xml:id="d365-f1"/> and 4th<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d365-f2"/> (dated 2d and 3d) instant and communicated without
                    delay to the minister of foreign affairs, who appreciates these communications
                    and is thankful for being kept informed of our intentions.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Horace Porter.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
